ers' testimony.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga43_2015__ci01.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}},{"id":"bco:35-4--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-09.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-09.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Myers v. Illiana Presbytery","year":2024,"disposition":"granted","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-09.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-09.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:35-4--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-09.md:occ-5281c90af34c","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-09.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-09.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":316},"excerpt":"…35-1) change – or the number of witnesses required to substantiate a charge (BCO 35-4) be altered?","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-09.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["elevation of censure","excommunication","deposition from office","indefinite suspension from sacraments","due process in church discipline","contumacy","incorrigibility","judicial process vs. parliamentary process","de novo trial","censure without additional process"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2023-9"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"An elder appealed Presbytery’s elevation, without additional process, of suspensions from office and the Sacraments to deposition and excommunication. The SJC granted the appeal, reversed in whole, and remanded, restoring the prior suspensions. Elevation required a hearing on incorrigibility and contumacy—with a charge, evidence, plea, and defense—but not a full de novo trial; disagreement with the original verdict alone was insufficient. The SJC left unresolved deposition from office when excommunication is absent."}},{"id":"bco:35-4--case:cases/ga29_2001__2000-02.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga29_2001__2000-02.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Adams v. Northeast Presbytery","year":2001,"disposition":"out_of_order","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga29_2001__2000-02.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga29_2001__2000-02.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:35-4--case:cases/ga29_2001__2000-02.md:occ-a5c4cb13e587","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga29_2001__2000-02.html","repository_path":"cases/ga29_2001__2000-02.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga29_2001__2000-02.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["complaint during appeal","appellate review","acquittal","retrial","administratively out of order","judicial procedure"],"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2000-2"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"A prosecutor's complaint relating to Northeast Presbytery's judicial case was held administratively out of order by the SJC. The SJC adopted two grounds: BCO 43-1 bars a complaint about a matter subject to an appeal in another case, and the complaint sought retrial of an accused on charges of which he had been acquitted, relief the SJC could not grant. Although the related appeal was later withdrawn and the withdrawal approved, the SJC still applied BCO 43-1. A concurrence disputed that first ground and urged BCO clarification of appellate review of acquittals. No merits ruling was made."}}],"history":[]}
